  "summary": "Screened all 52 clients with the all-client views (updates, performance, drift, feature tails, subgroup outcomes for Sex, AgeGroup and Income), then confirmed with narrower queries. Three clients (AZ, IA, MN) show a consistent sign-flipped/poisoned update signature: strongly negative cosine to the median update from the start, with no other client below about -0.2. AZ's per-round check confirms onset at round 1. I reported these as poisoning. I did not report several weaker leads, because each was a single noise-level flag or was contradicted by another tool: DE GenHlth tail/mean pattern (z_noise -4.97, but round 1 looks normal and drift shows no GenHlth shift); WV's binary-feature tails (AnyHealthcare p01 z_noise -6.06, which the guidance says is often noise on 0/1 features); WA's larger update norm (z=+4.1, with a high cosine and no other corroboration); GU's small-sample flags (citl z=-3.5, subgroup z_noise 3.3); VI's late DiffWalk drift (no flag); and CT's AgeGroup-12 O/E outlier (z_noise 4.47, inconsistent with CT's overall prevalence). Budget spent: 20.0 of 20.0 (none left unspent)."
